cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
title: "Volatility generalisation: learning-rate adaptation across volatile and stable environments"
version: 0.1.0
# The code is under the MIT licence; the data and results files are under CC BY 4.0.
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/the-wise-lab/volatility-generalisation-public"
abstract: >-
  Code and data for a study of how learning rates adapt when people move
  between volatile and stable environments. Participants did a
  probabilistic-choice task in four versions, each made of two sequential
  blocks. Five learning models are fitted to each condition. The fitted
  learning rates are then related to questionnaire measures.
keywords:
  - learning rate
  - volatility
  - reinforcement learning
  - computational modelling
  - Bayesian modelling
